        prompts: {
          human: "Welcome to Gaigel, where German tradition meets strategy. You and your partner must work together to reach 101 points first. Early in the hand, you can play any cardâ€”use this freedom wisely. When the Talon runs dry, you must follow suit or trump. Declare marriages (matching King and Ober) for 20 or 40 points. Count carefully, and call 'Out!' when you believe you've reached 101.",
          ai: 'Game: Gaigel (German trick-taking). Setup: 4 players in two partnerships. 48-card German deck (WÃ¼rttemberg pattern). 12 cards dealt (3 then 2 batches). 21st card shown as trump. Gameplay: Two phases: (1) Talon phase: players can play any card, no suit-following. (2) Talon empty: must follow suit, must trump if unable. Marriages (K+O of same suit) declare for 20 (non-trump) or 40 (trump) points. Scoring: Ace=11, 10=10, K=4, O=3, U=2, 7=0. Win: First team to 101 points.',
        },
